      "problem": "What is the distance between the points $(-4\\sqrt{5},-2\\sqrt{5})$ and $(\\sqrt{5},-12\\sqrt{5})?$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we have ${{(-4\\sqrt{5},-2\\sqrt{5})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(\\sqrt{5},-12\\sqrt{5})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\nSo, the distance $d$ can be calculated using the distance formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{5}-(-4\\sqrt{5}))}^{2}+{(-12\\sqrt{5}-(-2\\sqrt{5}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5\\sqrt{5})^{2}+(-10\\sqrt{5})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25(5)+100(5)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125+500} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{625} \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$",
